Self-check passes — `grep -n "loader"` returns only the three new/updated rules (lines 888, 895, 896), nothing else.

**Summary:** I replaced the single-line `.loader` rule in `system/styles.css` with a centered full-screen overlay and its supporting rules. `.loader` is now `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 1000` with a flex column layout (`align-items/justify-content: center`, `gap: var(--s2)`), a light-theme background of `rgba(238, 242, 247, .7)` (the project's `--bg` at 70% opacity), and it retains the original `color: var(--muted)` and `text-align: center` so index.html's static "Loading…" text still reads as a loading message. I added an `html[data-theme="dark"] .loader` override setting the background to `rgba(13, 21, 31, .7)` using the same dark-selector pattern already used elsewhere in the file, plus a `.loader-ring` child rule (36px ring via `border: 3px solid var(--line-strong)` + `border-top-color: var(--blue)`, `border-radius: 50%`) that reuses the file's existing `wvn-spin` keyframe rather than duplicating an identical one. No print CSS was added, and no other selector or rule was touched.
